    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP today, the offensive engine is anchored by our high-upside outfield. **James Wood** (78.42) and **Corbin Carroll** (75.42) are our premier starts; **James Wood** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and favorable situational speed metrics against a slow-delivering pitcher, while **Corbin Carroll** remains an elite play despite a slight park penalty, thanks to his plus matchup against Nick Martinez. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) also surges into must-start territory, fueled by a 14% platoon edge and a perfect 100% stolen base opportunity against Taj Bradley\u2019s delivery. We are also capitalizing on **Tyler Soderstrom** (71.48), whose R/R platoon splits are perfectly aligned for a high-efficiency outing against Walbert Ure\u00f1a.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Travis Bazzana** (51.16) on the bench. While his leadoff projection is strong, he fell just short of displacing **Zach McKinstry** (53.95) or **Max Muncy** (53.71), both of whom are projected for higher base production and favorable SP skill matchups today. We are monitoring two critical risk factors: the 45% rain probability hanging over the games featuring **Jose Caballero** and **James Wood**. Should those contests be postponed, we are prepared to pivot to our bench assets. While we remain aggressive on the basepaths, we are cautious of the \"Elite Hold\" catchers and pitchers facing **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero**, as their projected stolen base efficiency is suppressed by these specific defensive batteries.",
